  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To support the advocacy and lobbying work aimed at protecting the Awa people and their territory</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CIMI is a service agency of the National Conference of Brazilian Bishops (CNBB) formed in 1972 to provide training, advice and support to indigenous people and organisations, and to promote their rights. This project with the Maranhao branch of CIMI,  provides literacy training to all the Guaj&#xE1; in their own language as means of preserving and strengthening cultural values and in the Portuguese language to leaders so that they can communicate with wider Brazilian society, and thus defend and vindicate their rights. It also addresses the issues of healthcare, education, self-sufficiency and land rights.</narrative>
  </description>
